  "slug": "quantum-rydberg-6779",
  "summary": "Seven November preprints advance control for entangling gates, mediator qubits and state preparation, including a Rydberg phase-estimation demonstration on 19 atoms.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is control design for multi-qubit and mediator-mediated operations. One preprint proposes an analytically specified CCZ gate for neutral atoms under finite Rydberg interactions, compared with a fast antiblockade scheme. Another proposes reset-assisted control, analyzed with quantum trajectories, in which noisy mediator qubits drive high-fidelity gates on long-lived data qubits. The geodesiq package combines adiabatic and diabatic control for state transfer. Krotov optimization with a single local field prepares GHZ-type states in an XXZ chain, with fidelities above 0.927. An analog Rydberg simulator performs phase estimation on up to 19 atoms via Loschmidt echoes. Peripheral items cover bosonic Fock-state stabilization through Fock-space currents and a proposed Fe2+:forsterite qubit simulated at 99.9% fidelity. All results here are preprints, and most are proposals or simulations.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
